{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791601223,"nonce":"eKKfnrpeg/jbvGEKfrhixgsEk7k=","message":"Decision: stored unmatched rejection emails are re-matched (match.rematch_rejections) when a confirmation proposal is accepted and after every mail match scan: same employer_norm, not older than the application minus one day, and the same title or no title while it is the only application at that employer; it links the row and stores a rejected add_event proposal. Not wired to the detail page Did you apply yes answer. Reason: that path sets applied_at to the click time, which usually postdates the rejection, so the time check would reject it; the scan-time pass covers applications once they exist. On a real DB copy this links the one known missed case to its application.","files":null}]}